.\" incrmit man page. Source: doc/man/incrmit.1
.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt INCRMIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm incrmit
.Nd increment semantic versions across one or more files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm incrmit
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl M | m | p
.Op Fl r | e Ar id
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Op Fl d
.Pp
.Nm incrmit
.Cm discover
.Op Fl P Ar path
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Op Fl d
.Pp
.Nm incrmit
.Cm undo
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl d
.Pp
.Nm incrmit
.Cm version
.Pp
.Nm incrmit
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Op Fl -no-banner
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a TOML configuration file that lists one or more target files containing a
semantic version
.Pq MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH ,
locates the version token in each file, increments the major, minor, or patch
component, and writes the new value back atomically.
Only the version token is changed; surrounding file contents and permissions
are preserved.
.Pp
When no subcommand is given, the default action is to bump versions in the
configured files.
.Sh VERSION GRAMMAR
A version token is
.Sy [v]MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-PRERELEASE][+BUILD] ,
following semver 2.0.0: an optional single leading
.Sq v
or
.Sq V ,
three numeric components, and the optional prerelease and build-metadata
sections, each a dot-separated list of identifiers made of ASCII letters,
digits, and hyphens
.Pq a numeric prerelease identifier may not carry a leading zero .
The whole token is matched and rewritten as a unit, so
.Sy 1.2.3-rc.1
is never mistaken for the
.Sy 1.2.3
inside it.
.Pp
A version welded into a longer hyphen-joined word keeps only its numbers, since
a hyphen is also a legal prerelease character and
.Sy incrmit-1.2.3-linux-amd64.tar.gz
would otherwise be read as one token and rewritten whole.
Such a filename therefore bumps to
.Sy incrmit-1.2.4-linux-amd64.tar.gz ,
while a version standing on its own keeps its full token.
.Pp
A running prerelease is recorded in its own
.Sy prerelease
key in
.Pa incrmit.toml
(and build metadata in
.Sy build ) ,
which says outright which suffix belongs to the version rather than leaving it
to be guessed from the text.
With one recorded,
.Fl -release
promotes a prerelease inside a filename too
.Pq Sy app-1.2.3-rc.1.zip No -> Sy app-1.2.3.zip ;
without a config to consult, as in
.Fl -file
mode, only the numbers there are rewritten.
Any bump that drops the prerelease removes the key as well.
.Pp
A
.Fl M ,
.Fl m ,
or
.Fl p
bump drops both sections:
.Sy 1.2.3-rc.1
patches to
.Sy 1.2.4 ,
not
.Sy 1.2.4-rc.1 .
Build metadata is never carried forward.
Use
.Fl -release
to promote a prerelease in place and
.Fl -pre
to start or advance one.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm bump
Default command.
Bump the semantic version in configured files.
.It Cm discover
Scan a directory tree for version-bearing files and write
.Pa incrmit.toml .
The scan stays inside the directory it is given: symlinks are never followed,
only regular files are read
.Pq never pipes, devices, or sockets ,
and files larger than 32 MiB are skipped
.Pq see Fl -max-file-size .
.It Cm undo
Revert the most recent bump, restoring the previous version in every file it
changed and in
.Pa incrmit.toml .
The bump history is read from a state file kept next to the config
.Pq Pa .incrmit.state.toml .
A file edited since the bump is left untouched and the undo is refused.
Repeated undos walk back through successive bumps.
.It Cm version
Print the
.Nm
tool version.
The
.Fl version ,
.Fl v ,
and
.Fl -version
flags are aliases.
.It Cm help
Show an overview, or detailed help for
.Cm bump ,
.Cm discover ,
.Cm undo ,
.Cm version ,
or
.Cm help .
The overview is printed under a plain ASCII banner; see
.Fl -no-banner .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , Fl -config Ar path
Path to the TOML config file.
Default:
.Pa incrmit.toml .
.It Fl f , Fl -file Ar path
Bump the version in a single file, skipping the config.
.It Fl M , Fl -major
Bump the major version (resets minor and patch).
.It Fl m , Fl -minor
Bump the minor version (resets patch).
.It Fl p , Fl -patch
Bump the patch version.
This is the default when no major/minor flag is given.
If more than one of
.Fl M ,
.Fl m ,
and
.Fl p
is supplied, the highest component wins
.Pq major > minor > patch .
.It Fl r , Fl -release
Promote a prerelease to the release it names, without changing the numbers:
.Sy 1.2.3-rc.1
becomes
.Sy 1.2.3 .
Build metadata is dropped with it.
It is a usage error
.Pq exit 2
on a version that has no prerelease, or together with
.Fl -pre
or a component flag.
.It Fl e , Fl -pre Ar id
Start or advance a prerelease of series
.Ar id
.Pq for example Ar rc .
Off a release this bumps the patch first
.Pq Sy 1.2.3 No -> Sy 1.2.4-rc.1 ;
within the same series it advances the counter
.Pq Sy 1.2.4-rc.1 No -> Sy 1.2.4-rc.2 ;
in a different series it restarts on the same numbers
.Pq Sy 1.2.4-beta.2 No -> Sy 1.2.4-rc.1 .
Naming a component alongside it opens a new release line instead, so
.Fl m Fl -pre Ar rc
gives
.Sy 1.3.0-rc.1 .
The
.Ar id
must be a valid prerelease identifier list; anything else is a usage error
.Pq exit 2 .
.It Fl s , Fl -max-file-size Ar size
Largest file to read.
A
.Ar size
is a plain byte count
.Pq 1048576
or a value with a unit suffix such as
.Ar 512KB ,
.Ar 32MiB ,
or
.Ar 2G ;
a size of
.Ar 0
means no limit.
For the default command, a target over the limit is reported as an error and
nothing is written; the default is no limit.
For
.Cm discover ,
a file over the limit is skipped; the default is 32MiB.
.It Fl d , Fl -dry-run
Print the new version without writing files.
.It Fl P , Fl -path Ar dir
.Dq discover only.
Root directory to scan.
Default: current directory.
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar path
.Dq discover only.
Path for the generated config.
Default:
.Pa incrmit.toml .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
For the default command and
.Cm discover ,
explicit help is printed to stdout; usage errors print help to stderr.
.It Fl -no-banner
Omit the ASCII banner printed above the top-level overview.
Accepted by
.Cm help
and by top-level
.Fl h
and
.Fl -help ,
which are the only commands that print the banner.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa incrmit.toml
Default configuration listing target files and optional pinned version values.
A pinned version is written as up to three keys —
.Sy version
(the numeric core),
.Sy prerelease ,
and
.Sy build .
A token written whole in
.Sy version
.Pq Qq 1.2.3-rc.1
is still accepted and is split on the next rewrite.
.It Pa .incrmit.state.toml
Bump-history state file written next to the config after a bump, used by
.Cm undo .
It is local, tool-maintained working state and is not meant to be committed
.Pq add it to Pa .gitignore .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Generic runtime error (for example missing config or filesystem error).
.It 2
Invalid arguments or flags.
.It 3
No version found, or an ambiguous or unparseable version.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Bump the patch version in all configured files:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit
.Pp
Preview a minor bump without writing:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit -m -d
.Pp
Start a release candidate, then iterate on it, then ship it:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit --pre rc
.Dl "# 1.2.3 -> 1.2.4-rc.1"
.Dl incrmit --pre rc
.Dl "# 1.2.4-rc.1 -> 1.2.4-rc.2"
.Dl incrmit --release
.Dl "# 1.2.4-rc.2 -> 1.2.4"
.Pp
Generate a config from the current tree:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit discover
.Pp
Revert the most recent bump:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit undo
.Pp
Preview an undo without writing:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit undo -d
.Pp
Show tool version:
.Pp
.Dl incrmit version
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://github.com/sasmaq/incrmit
